{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information includes the probabilities and maximum outcomes of both lotteries. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 3000 Euros with a 25% probability, while Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 4000 Euros with a 20% probability. The difference in probabilities (25% vs. 20%) is small (5 percentage points), which may be considered negligible as per the reason. The reason evaluates the maximum outcomes and prefers the lottery with the higher maximum (4000 Euros) if the probability difference is negligible. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery B.",
